Daddy Deployment Checklist (for www.videocourts.com)To host this fully functional system (not just the static HTML pilot) on GoDaddy, you cannot use basic "Shared Hosting" (cPanel). You need a VPS (Virtual Private Server) or Managed WordPress/Node.js Hosting to run the backend and WebRTC signaling.p 1: Domain & DNSPurchase videocourts.com on GoDaddy.Point the A Record to your GoDaddy VPS IP address.Enable Free SSL (Let's Encrypt) in GoDaddy cPanel/Security for HTTPS (mandatory for WebRTC and ID.me).Step 2: Server Environment (GoDaddy VPS)Provision a GoDaddy VPS (Ubuntu 22.04 LTS, minimum 4GB RAM, 2 vCPUs).Install Node.js (v18+) and PM2 (to keep the backend running).Install Nginx as a reverse proxy (to route videocourts.com to your Node.js app and handle SSL).tall PostgreSQL (for user/case data) and Redis (for WebRTC signaling/sessions).Step 3: WebRTC / Video InfrastructureDo not host the actual video traffic on the GoDaddy VPS. It will bottleneck immediately.Sign up for LiveKit Cloud or Agora.io (both have generous free tiers).Get your API Key and Secret.Your GoDaddy backend will generate a secure token and pass it to the frontend video.js player to connect the judge, attorney, and defendant.